Module 5: Form Elements & Input Validations (Deep Dive)

HTML5 Form sirf data lene ke liye nahi hote, ye browser ke andar hi user ki galat galtiyon ko rokte hain (bina complex programming ke).

1. The <from> Action & Method
<form action="submit_data.php" method="POST">

:: Action: jab user submit button dabayega, toh yeh saara data kisi file ya server ke pass jayega, wo address yahan likha jata hain.
::Method: Data bhejne ke do tareeqe hain:
    ::GET: ye data ko browser ke URL bar mein upar dikha deta hain(security ke liye kharab hai. search box ke liye accha hai).
    ::POST: ye data ko piche se (hidden tarike se) bhejta hai (passwords aur personal data ke liye hamesha POST use hota hai).



2.PowerFul HTML5 Validation Attributes
::required: isko input tag mein likh dene se user us dabbe ko khali     chhod sakta.

::pattern (Regular Expression): Sabse advanced validation! Agar aap chahte hain ki user sirf 10 digit ka mobile number hi dale, toh aap pattern set kar sakte hain:

<input type="tel" pattern="[0-9]{10}" placeholder="10 Digit Number">

::min aur max: Numbers ya dates par limits lagane k liye. jaise agar umar 18 se 60 ke beech honi chahiye:

<input type="tel" pattern="[0-9]{10}" placeholder="10 Digit Number">